James asked how to send an email from Python for personal notification purposes without being filtered as spam. I provided a code sample using the `smtplib` and `email` libraries to send a basic email, highlighting tips like using app passwords and maintaining proper headers to avoid spam filters. He then inquired about a more straightforward notification method on his Mac. I suggested using `osascript` with a Python script to create macOS notifications, offering a code example and explaining how to customize the title and message. This approach was presented as a lightweight alternative to emailing.
